"faq": [
["Does this course teach me to predict prices?", "No. It teaches a traditional method, its rules, and how to test its indications against recorded prices. Whatever you write down is a hypothesis, and nothing is guaranteed."],
["Why is there no calculation on Day 1?", "A system with many dependent steps needs a map first. The manual sets the Day 1 competency as explaining the entire system without advanced calculation."],
["Can I use this together with my regular astrology tools?", "The manual cautions that general astrology and Argh Nirupan should not be mixed without a clearly established rule. Keep them in separate notebooks."],
["Who is Narapati and what is the Jal Yoga link?", "The manuscript names them, but the available passage does not give the detail. The course does not fill the gap from memory. Mark it 'confirm from the original manuscript'."],
["Is Brahmayamala a book I can obtain?", "The manual cites it as the source of the opening verse. This course does not give bibliographic details beyond the manual. Consult the instructor or the original manuscript if you wish to trace it."],
["Why is the gold example in the lesson if gold has no stated lord?", "It explains the order of work only. The manual says the example asserts no planetary ownership and no gold-price result."],
["How many cases do I need before I trust a rule?", "There is no fixed number in the source. Statistically, a single case proves nothing, so build a long record and judge it honestly, including the failures."]
],
