["p", "A learner submits a sheet. Measurements are HYPOTHETICAL and used only to practise the checklist."],
["p", "Record on the sheet: outer square 18 cm by 18 cm; ten vertical lines at 0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16 and 18 cm; horizontal lines measured at 0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 13, 16 and 18 cm."],
["ol", "Count vertical lines: 10, so vertical intervals: 9. Pass|Count horizontal lines: 10, so horizontal intervals: 9. Pass|Check vertical spacing: every gap is 2 cm. Pass|Check horizontal spacing: gaps are 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 3, 2. Two gaps are wrong (1 cm and 3 cm)|Cells: 9 x 9 = 81 in count, but not of equal dimensions. Fail|Correct the line at 13 cm to 14 cm. The gaps become 2 cm each. Re-measure|Mark main and intermediate directions according to the original diagram, and confirm orientation by comparing with the master copy|Pass all nine checklist items and sign the sheet with date"],
["p", "Lesson: a grid can have the right number of lines and still fail. Counting alone is not verification. Measuring is."]
