"faq": [
["What are the names of the three Vedha categories?","The extract used in this course says there are three but does not name them. Take the names from the original passage and diagram, and do not use names from another Vedha system."],
["Does a Vakri planet always give the opposite direction of a Margi planet?","The extract does not say so. The manual only says the direction depends on motion and must be checked against the source. Do not assume a mirror image."],
["Is Vedha a good or a bad sign?","Neither is stated in the Day 6 text. Vedha is an identification. Any good or bad reading belongs to a later interpretative stage and its own rules."],
["Why do I need the Pada if I already know the Nakshatra?","The manual lists the Pada as a required input. A Nakshatra spans 13 degrees 20 minutes and a Pada 3 degrees 20 minutes, so two longitudes in the same Nakshatra can differ in Pada, and special rules for corner positions refer to the first or last Pada."],
["Which ayanamsha should I use?","The manual does not specify in the extract. Use one convention consistently, write it in the worksheet, and be aware that near a Pada boundary a small difference can change the Pada."],
["Can I fill the Vedhya cell from the Day 1 to 4 Chakra I constructed?","Only after reading the rule from the original passage. Your Chakra provides the cells. The rule says which cell is pierced by which planet and direction."],
["How is a Vedha record connected to commodity prices?","It is not connected on Day 6. Commodity interpretation uses Desh, Kaal, Panya, lords, strength and Phala rules, taught from Day 9 onwards."]
],
